   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The annual report for year 4 (2024) is expected in September 2025. 

Globally, the IRC reached 34,5 million people in 2023 using 1,5 billion USD, with Sida funding reaching 4,25 million people. 
The annual report for year 3 included 14 humanitarian country responses delivered using the Programme Based Approach (PBA), 11 Rapid Response Mechanism (RRM) projects, and seven Methods and Capacity Development projects, including the InterAction  grant and support to the Lebanon and Libya INGO Forums.
During Year 3, IRC humanitarian programs using the PBA reached over 4 million people, representing a substantial increase of 57% from the previous year. The Rapid Response Mechanism supported close to 238,000 individuals in acute crises, with women and girls representing 57% of the RRM reach and 62% of the PBA total reach.</narrative>
